# URAE Mathematics Notepad: Stochastic Itô Calculus & SDEs
# Interactive continuous document for Itô's Lemma, quadratic variation, geometric Brownian motion, and Black-Scholes PDE derivation.

# Parameters for Geometric Brownian Motion
mu: Parameter = 0.05 [s^-1]
sigma: Parameter = 0.20 [s^-0.5]
S0: Parameter = 100.0 [USD]

# Time and process variables
t: Variable
S: Variable
W_t: Variable

# Domain constraints
{ S in Reals | S > 0.0 }
{ t in Reals | t >= 0.0 }

# 1. Quadratic Variation & Itô Differential Multiplication Rules
# (dt)^2 = 0, dt * dW_t = 0, (dW_t)^2 = dt
ito_rule_dt_dt = ito_mult(dt, dt)
ito_rule_dt_dw = ito_mult(dt, dW_t)
ito_rule_dw_dw = ito_mult(dW_t, dW_t)

# 2. Geometric Brownian Motion (GBM) SDE
# dS_t = mu * S_t * dt + sigma * S_t * dW_t
dS_t = mu * S * dt + sigma * S * dW_t

# 3. Application of Itô's Lemma to f(S) = ln(S)
# df = (f'(S) * mu * S + 1/2 * f''(S) * sigma^2 * S^2) * dt + f'(S) * sigma * S * dW_t
# Since d(ln S)/dS = 1/S and d^2(ln S)/dS^2 = -1/S^2:
# d(ln S) = (mu - 1/2 * sigma^2) * dt + sigma * dW_t
d_ln_S = ito_lemma(ln(S), S, mu * S, sigma * S)

# 4. Black-Scholes Differential Operator & Option Pricing PDE
r: Parameter = 0.03 [s^-1]
V: Function(S, t)
bs_pde = diff(V(S, t), t) + r * S * diff(V(S, t), S) + 0.5 * sigma^2 * S^2 * diff(diff(V(S, t), S), S) - r * V(S, t)
